  "paper_text": "The paper says co-occurrence is controlled by the distance between word occurrences and connects lexical units occurring within a window of maximum N words; it then says edges are added between filtered lexical units that co-occur within a window of N words. It does not explicitly define whether filtered-out tokens count toward that N or whether N is a maximum positional distance versus the width of a token window.",
  "interpretations": {
    "raw_token_window_width": "Current implementation: eligible vertices are connected only when their original token positions lie in the same N-token-wide window (maximum positional difference N-1).",
    "raw_max_distance": "Alternative: count all original tokens but permit a maximum position difference of N (an N+1-token span).",
    "filtered_token_window_width": "Alternative: remove ineligible token occurrences first, then apply an N-token-wide window over the eligible sequence."
  },
